Facts found in this image (30231 compressed inodes, sealed volume, case-insensitive): signature "fpmc" (0x636d7066);
decmpfs xattr is embedded (flags 2); no dstream xfield and no extents; inode has HAS_UNCOMPRESSED_SIZE with size equal to
the decmpfs size, and NO_RSRC_FORK for inline files or HAS_RSRC_FORK for resource ones; types seen: 8 (25500) and 9 (4731).
Type 8 resource fork: u32 little endian offset table (blocks+1 entries), blocks back to back, last offset = fork size,
blocks = ceil(size/64K); the fork is always a stream xattr, even when small. Sealed volumes keep file extents in the fext tree
and hashed index nodes hold child = value + root oid.
